{
  "components": {
    "schemas": {
      "AgentListResponse": {
        "description": "Every agent this deployment is configured with, in configuration order.",
        "properties": {
          "items": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AgentSummary"
            },
            "title": "Items",
            "type": "array"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "items"
        ],
        "title": "AgentListResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "AgentSummary": {
        "description": "One agent, as the picker on an empty chat offers it.\n\nThree fields, and deliberately no more: **no system prompt** -- it is the\noperator's, it is not a message and it never leaves the process\n(``docs/specs/conversations.md``) -- and no vendor, endpoint or key. The\nmodel is not here either: which model an agent runs is the operator's\nchoice and shows on the answers it produced (``ProvenanceView``), where it\nis a fact about what happened rather than something to pick by.",
        "properties": {
          "engine": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Engine"
          },
          "id": {
            "title": "Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id",
          "title",
          "engine"
        ],
        "title": "AgentSummary",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "Channel": {
        "description": "Where a message came from (``docs/specs/channels.md``).\n\nA conversation is not tied to one: each message records its own, so a\nconversation begun in the web UI and continued from somewhere else says\nwhich was which. Other channels join this enum with the bridge that\nserves them; a stored ``web`` never changes meaning.",
        "enum": [
          "web"
        ],
        "title": "Channel",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "ContentPart": {
        "description": "One piece of a message's content, named by its kind.\n\n``kind`` is the discriminator the stored format uses\n(``docs/specs/conversations.md``), so a client reads the kinds it knows and\ncan be given another without the shape moving. Text is the only kind this\nbuild sends (``SentKind``); ``text`` is the whole of it.",
        "properties": {
          "kind": {
            "const": "text",
            "title": "Kind",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "text": {
            "title": "Text",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "kind",
          "text"
        ],
        "title": "ContentPart",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ConversationListResponse": {
        "description": "One page of the caller's conversations, and how to ask for the next.\n\n``next_cursor`` is ``null`` on the last page. It is opaque: a position\ninside this person's own listing, written by the store and read by it, and\nnothing a client should take apart (``docs/specs/conversations.md``).",
        "properties": {
          "items": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ConversationSummary"
            },
            "title": "Items",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "next_cursor": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Next Cursor"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "items",
          "next_cursor"
        ],
        "title": "ConversationListResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ConversationSummary": {
        "description": "A conversation as the panel lists it and as a write answers with it.\n\nNo owner: it is the person asking, on every route there is\n(``docs/specs/privacy.md``). ``active_leaf_id`` is the position its author\nis at, which is what ``PUT /api/conversations/{id}/leaf`` moves.",
        "properties": {
          "active_leaf_id": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "format": "uuid",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Active Leaf Id"
          },
          "agent": {
            "title": "Agent",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "created_at": {
            "format": "date-time",
            "title": "Created At",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "id": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "title": "Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "updated_at": {
            "format": "date-time",
            "title": "Updated At",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id",
          "title",
          "agent",
          "created_at",
          "updated_at",
          "active_leaf_id"
        ],
        "title": "ConversationSummary",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "EndedBadlyView": {
        "description": "The last run of the conversation, when it failed, was cancelled or was interrupted.\n\nSo that a reload after an answer went wrong says so, instead of showing a\nturn that simply stops (``docs/specs/runs.md``).\n\n``state`` is the whole of the reason, and it is the only one the platform\nrecords as a **kind**: what else a run holds is ``error``, free text made\nout of whatever a provider or a traceback said, written for an operator.\nIt stays on the record and in the log, like the detail of every other\nrefusal (``robinauts.api.errors``).",
        "properties": {
          "ended_at": {
            "format": "date-time",
            "title": "Ended At",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "run_id": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "title": "Run Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "state": {
            "enum": [
              "cancelled",
              "failed",
              "interrupted"
            ],
            "title": "State",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "run_id",
          "state",
          "ended_at"
        ],
        "title": "EndedBadlyView",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "Engine": {
        "description": "The agent frameworks a turn can be run by (``docs/specs/agents.md``).\n\nA property of the agent, recorded on every message, so that a conversation\nsays which engine produced which answer after the agent has been changed.\nThe values are the ones the configuration is written with.",
        "enum": [
          "langgraph",
          "pydantic-ai"
        ],
        "title": "Engine",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "ErrorResponse": {
        "description": "Every refusal, in one shape (``robinauts.api.errors``).",
        "properties": {
          "detail": {
            "title": "Detail",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "error": {
            "title": "Error",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "error",
          "detail"
        ],
        "title": "ErrorResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "HealthResponse": {
        "description": "What ``GET /health`` answers. It holds no data and says nothing else.",
        "properties": {
          "status": {
            "title": "Status",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "status"
        ],
        "title": "HealthResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "MessageView": {
        "description": "One message of a conversation, with what places it in the tree.\n\n``parent_id`` is what makes this a tree and not a list: it is ``None`` for\na root, and a client walks it upwards to have a branch. **Reasoning is not\nhere**: see ``of``.",
        "properties": {
          "channel": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Channel"
          },
          "created_at": {
            "format": "date-time",
            "title": "Created At",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "id": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "title": "Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "parent_id": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "format": "uuid",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Parent Id"
          },
          "parts": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ContentPart"
            },
            "title": "Parts",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProvenanceView"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "role": {
            "enum": [
              "assistant",
              "user"
            ],
            "title": "Role",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id",
          "parent_id",
          "role",
          "channel",
          "created_at",
          "parts",
          "provenance"
        ],
        "title": "MessageView",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "OpenedConversationResponse": {
        "description": "A conversation opened: one moment of it, with everything drawing it needs.\n\n``messages`` is **every message of the tree**, oldest first with ties\nbroken by id, so the branches beside the one being shown are there to\nswitch to without a second request. Each carries its ``parent_id``, and\n``leaf_id`` is the message the conversation opens on\n(``docs/specs/conversations.md``): the branch is the walk from that id up\nthe parents, which the client does and the server does not send twice.\n\n``run_id`` and ``resume`` are there when a run is in flight, and\n``ended_badly`` instead when the last one ended badly. Never both: what\nmatters about a run that is going is the run.",
        "properties": {
          "conversation": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ConversationSummary"
          },
          "ended_badly": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EndedBadlyView"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "leaf_id": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "format": "uuid",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Leaf Id"
          },
          "messages": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MessageView"
            },
            "title": "Messages",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "resume": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ResumeView"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "run_id": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "format": "uuid",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Run Id"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "conversation",
          "messages",
          "leaf_id",
          "run_id",
          "resume",
          "ended_badly"
        ],
        "title": "OpenedConversationResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ProvenanceView": {
        "description": "What an answer records: the agent, the engine, the model and the run.\n\nOn an assistant message and on no other (``domain.Message``). The model is\nthe platform's own id for it -- what the configuration calls it -- and no\nvendor, endpoint or key is anywhere near the wire.",
        "properties": {
          "agent": {
            "title": "Agent",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "engine": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Engine"
          },
          "model": {
            "title": "Model",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "run_id": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "title": "Run Id",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "agent",
          "engine",
          "model",
          "run_id"
        ],
        "title": "ProvenanceView",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ProviderSummary": {
        "description": "One provider to offer a sign-in button for. No secret, no endpoint.",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "title": "Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id",
          "title"
        ],
        "title": "ProviderSummary",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "RenameRequest": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "A new title for a conversation. A renamed title is never overwritten.\n\nThe bound is the record's own (``domain.MAX_TITLE_CHARS``), said here so\nthat it is **in the document**: a client that knows how long a title may\nbe can say so in its own form, instead of finding out by being refused.\nWhat the length cannot say -- one line, printable, and something other\nthan spaces -- is the application's, and is refused there\n(``application.Conversations.rename``).",
        "properties": {
          "title": {
            "maxLength": 120,
            "minLength": 1,
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "title"
        ],
        "title": "RenameRequest",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ResumeView": {
        "description": "Where to attach to the run in flight, and what its next message follows.\n\n``after`` is the position to carry on from and ``follows`` is the id the\nnext message announced after it will hang under -- the two things a\nwatcher of that stream is checked with, handed over together so that\nneither is guessed (``docs/specs/runs.md``).",
        "properties": {
          "after": {
            "title": "After",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "follows": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "format": "uuid",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Follows"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "after",
          "follows"
        ],
        "title": "ResumeView",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "RunState": {
        "description": "Where a run is (``docs/specs/runs.md``).",
        "enum": [
          "running",
          "waiting",
          "finished",
          "failed",
          "cancelled",
          "interrupted"
        ],
        "title": "RunState",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "RunView": {
        "description": "A run as a client sees it: where it got to, and when.\n\n``ended_at`` is what the record calls ``finished_at``: a run that failed,\nwas cancelled or was interrupted did not finish, and every ended run has\none. ``started_at`` is ``null`` until a process took the run up, and\n``ended_at`` until it ended. What went wrong is not here, for the reason\ngiven on ``EndedBadlyView``.",
        "properties": {
          "ended_at": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "format": "date-time",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Ended At"
          },
          "id": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "title": "Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "started_at": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "format": "date-time",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Started At"
          },
          "state": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RunState"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id",
          "state",
          "started_at",
          "ended_at"
        ],
        "title": "RunView",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "SelectLeafRequest": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "The message its author is now on; any message of the conversation.\n\nNot only the end of a branch: what is recorded is a position, and opening\nthe conversation resolves it to the branch below it\n(``docs/specs/conversations.md``).",
        "properties": {
          "message_id": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "title": "Message Id",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "message_id"
        ],
        "title": "SelectLeafRequest",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "SessionResponse": {
        "description": "What ``GET /auth/session`` answers, signed in or not.\n\n``sign_in`` is whether this deployment has a sign-in configuration at all;\nwithout one there are no providers and nobody to be.\n\n``local_development`` is the exception to that last part: the local\ndevelopment mode has no sign-in and no providers, and yet somebody *is*\nsigned in -- the one local user everything runs as. It is what the\ninterface shows its permanent banner for (``docs/specs/frontend.md``), and\nit is why the two are separate fields rather than one: \"nothing is\nconfigured\" and \"sign-in is deliberately off\" are different things to say\nto a person, and only the second one has a user with it.",
        "properties": {
          "local_development": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Local Development",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "providers": {
            "default": [],
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProviderSummary"
            },
            "title": "Providers",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "public_url": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Public Url"
          },
          "sign_in": {
            "title": "Sign In",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "user": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UserSummary"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "sign_in"
        ],
        "title": "SessionResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "UserSummary": {
        "description": "Who is signed in, as the interface shows them in the profile block.",
        "properties": {
          "email": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Email"
          },
          "id": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "title": "Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "name": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Name"
          },
          "provider": {
            "title": "Provider",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id",
          "provider"
        ],
        "title": "UserSummary",
        "type": "object"
      }
    }
  },
  "info": {
    "summary": "Conversational agents that play fair.",
    "title": "Robinauts",
    "version": "0"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/api/agents": {
      "get": {
        "description": "The agents this deployment is configured with, for the picker.\n\nThe id to start a conversation with, the title to show, and the engine it\nruns on. **Not the system prompt**, which is the operator's and is not a\nmessage, and nothing about a vendor or a key (``docs/specs/agents.md``).\n\nDeclared rather than injected: the list is the deployment's and is the\nsame for everybody signed in, so the route needs the declaration and not\nthe person.\n\nThey are fixed at start-up in this version: the configuration is read once\nby the composition root, so an agent added or removed shows here after a\nrestart.",
        "operationId": "list_agents_api_agents_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AgentListResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Forbidden"
          },
          "default": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "any other refusal, in the same shape: 400, 405, 500"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List Agents",
        "tags": [
          "agents"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/conversations": {
      "get": {
        "description": "The caller's conversations, most recently updated first, one page at a time.\n\n``limit`` is how many are wanted, and its bound is **in the document**:\nbetween 1 and ``application.MAX_PAGE``, which is what a store will page.\nA client can therefore hold itself to it instead of finding out by being\nrefused, and one outside it -- or not a whole number at all, an empty\n``?limit=`` included -- is refused naming the field and the rule and never\nthe number.\n\n``cursor`` is what the page before this one handed back as\n``next_cursor``, and is left out for the first page; an **empty** one is\nread as left out, since a client that sends no cursor and one that sends\nnothing in it are asking the same thing. One that does not parse is\nrefused as a value, naming the field.\n\nEither parameter **given twice** is refused rather than quietly read once\n(``given_once``).\n\nThe order is total: ties on ``updated_at`` are broken by id, so two\nconversations written in the same millisecond cannot swap places between\ntwo pages. What that does and does not promise is in this module's\ndocstring.",
        "operationId": "list_conversations_api_conversations_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "limit",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 30,
              "maximum": 100,
              "minimum": 1,
              "title": "Limit",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "cursor",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "Cursor"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ConversationListResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Forbidden"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Unprocessable Entity"
          },
          "default": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "any other refusal, in the same shape: 400, 405, 500"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List Conversations",
        "tags": [
          "conversations"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/conversations/{conversation_id}": {
      "delete": {
        "description": "Delete a conversation for good, with its messages, its runs and their events.\n\nThere is no trash in this version\n(``docs/working-notes/poc-scope.md``).\n\n**Not idempotent.** A conversation that is not there -- never was, already\ndeleted, or somebody else's -- is 404, like everything else that is not\nthere, because the application finds the conversation and checks who is\nasking before it deletes anything. So deleting twice is 204 and then 404,\nand a client that means \"make sure this is gone\" reads both as success.\n\n**A conversation with a run going is not deleted**: it is refused with 409\n(``RunAlreadyActiveError``), and its author cancels the run first. The\nstore decides that in the transaction that would have deleted, so there is\nno window for a run to begin in (``docs/specs/conversations.md``).",
        "operationId": "delete_conversation_api_conversations__conversation_id__delete",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "conversation_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "format": "uuid",
              "title": "Conversation Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Not Found"
          },
          "409": {
